{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes","id":1174885,"title":"Help developing a idea: \"Superheroes\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-10T09:25:05-08:00","id":1174885,"title":"Help developing a idea: \"Superheroes\"","content":"In my current Werewolf game, i am planning on having my PCs encounter a pschotic vigilante dressed as a Knight calling himself Paladin, who happened to target criminals the PCs are tracking. My idea is that Paladin ends up inspiring people to become costumed vigilantes, resulting in a situation similar to Kick-Ass. I would like help determining how the CWod would react to this development","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T09:42:02-08:00","id":1174891,"title":"","content":"How big a role do you want these people to play- are they antagonists? Foils? Random background noise?<br /> <br /> If these would-be 'superheroes' run afoul of a werewolf pack, they aren't going to live very long.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine these vigilantes would be treated like 'real world' superheros, I,E, no one cares and they are largely ineffectual. It could be a bit funny if they are murdering people in the name of 'justice,' and actually making situations worse... kind of like holding up a cracked mirror to the Garou's own position.<br /> <br /> There is always the opportunity to pit scrappy but misguided people against the Wyrm. Maybe some of these heroes try to take on what ends up being a fomori nest and they get their asses kicked... after they barely escape with their lives, a few enterprising banes visit them and offer them a chance to gain some <i>real</i> superpowers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T11:22:24-08:00","id":1174926,"title":"","content":"Wyld or Weaver Spirits could also take an interest in them to givd them power. Or sone could develop Numina and have &quot;real&quot; powers.<br /> <br /> Personaly I would go the &quot;bastard&quot; way and have Paladin be ghouled (bonus point for a Dominate Malkavian) and have super-strength, super-speed, super-senses, super-endurance, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T11:31:11-08:00","id":1174929,"title":"","content":"Vigilantes wouldn't last very long, though it'd be fun. <br /> <br /> Actual superheroes with super powers(like Superman, the Flash, or Martian Manhunter), would destroy entire packs on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T12:07:48-08:00","id":1174936,"title":"","content":"I intend for them to be a mix of foils and bacground noise. Paladin himself is introduced after he decapitates either a PENTEX exec or a gangster infront of the PCs. IAlso, spirits giving them powers sounds pretty cool. <br /> <br /> Paladin himself is a murderous vigilante whose alter-ego was a PENTEX accountant who was gunned down but somehow survived and is seeking revenge on both the subsidiary he worked for and the gangsters who gunned him down. Somehow, he ends up getting a internet following of people following in his footsetps and dispensing justice like their idol. But unlike him, a lot of them do it non-lethally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-10-2018, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T15:43:30-08:00","id":1175004,"title":"","content":"Why not make him an Imbued? Avenger or Wayward would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T15:50:20-08:00","id":1175005,"title":"","content":"I am using W20 rules so i am not sure how to make Imbued characters. But, him being one would maje sense, except he hunts crooks, not monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T17:23:36-08:00","id":1175028,"title":"","content":"What do you want to achieve with &quot;Paladin&quot; Because having a complete mortal doing this stuff is a pretty good way to have the werewolves reflect on their own actions.<br /> If he's spirit touched, they can rationalise that it's just another bane/drone/Ghoul, but the humanity of it should make for better roleplaying. And less likely to just kill him for being different.<br /> If you keep him mortal, you could look at unusual merits to represent the special-ness though.<br /> <br /> If you want him to have powers: stick to what you know, keep it as the werewolves understand. Gifts from spirits and the like. Crossing things over from other books can be difficult and you don't want to buy a whole book and get a new set of rules in your head for just one NPC","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T17:47:20-08:00","id":1175036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1174929#post1174929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vigilantes wouldn't last very long, though it'd be fun.<br /> <br /> Actual superheroes with super powers(like Superman, the Flash, or Martian Manhunter), would destroy entire packs on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep it street level with characters on the level of Captain America, Spiderman or Wolverine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T19:46:31-08:00","id":1175066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1174929#post1174929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vigilantes wouldn't last very long, though it'd be fun.<br /> <br /> Actual superheroes with super powers(like Superman, the Flash, or Martian Manhunter), would destroy entire packs on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. At least for DC, anyone that's not magical typically has to tread lightly around magical threats, on account of having no defense against them (even, oddly enough, Wonder Woman). Superman in particular gets a really harsh deal, because magic cuts through his defenses as easily as kryptonite, and everything in the WoD that has any modicum of power is probably what DC would consider magical. Superman could potentially fly out to wherever a Red Talon pack is, but just punching said RT and triggering a Rage recovery roll would potentially get Supes lethally mauled in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T19:55:38-08:00","id":1175068,"title":"","content":"Good points so far. So far, i like the idea of making Paladin a normal human. But, over time, some of the vigilanties he has inspired start getting powers of their own either through hedge magic, being kinfolk or spirits. I can understand why Banes and Weaver Spirits might take interest in costumed vigilanties, but why Wyld spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-10-2018, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T23:21:02-08:00","id":1175109,"title":"","content":"I'm going to suggest Paladin be a HIGH Willpower Formori. All the Bane really cares about is the rage and killing and torture the fact that Paladin is doing &quot;good' with it should give the players some food for thought on the Triat without having to go crossover heavy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T04:29:26-08:00","id":1175138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175066#post1175066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite. At least for DC, anyone that's not magical typically has to tread lightly around magical threats, on account of having no defense against them (even, oddly enough, Wonder Woman). Superman in particular gets a really harsh deal, because magic cuts through his defenses as easily as kryptonite, and everything in the WoD that has any modicum of power is probably what DC would consider magical. Superman could potentially fly out to wherever a Red Talon pack is, but just punching said RT and triggering a Rage recovery roll would potentially get Supes lethally mauled in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool. I'll just agree to disagree. <br /> <br /> Superman in particular is affected by magic on a totally different scale than most creatures in the WoD have at their disposal. But if you want, I can throw him out the window.<br /> <br /> DC superheroes are on an entirely different level of power. Wonder Woman, who has speed that makes Celerity look like someone treading in water, and the strength to punch through planets, would have a field day in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Same would Martian Manhunter. <br /> <br /> Green Lantern, the Flash, etc. are simply too powerful. And that's not even bothering to get into the villians.<br /> <br /> Release Doomsday into a caern, and you will believe a werewolf can fly. To the moon. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T06:01:11-08:00","id":1175144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175138#post1175138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cool. I'll just agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> Superman in particular is affected by magic on a totally different scale than most creatures in the WoD have at their disposal. But if you want, I can throw him out the window.<br /> <br /> DC superheroes are on an entirely different level of power. Wonder Woman, who has speed that makes Celerity look like someone treading in water, and the strength to punch through planets, would have a field day in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Same would Martian Manhunter.<br /> <br /> Green Lantern, the Flash, etc. are simply too powerful. And that's not even bothering to get into the villians.<br /> <br /> Release Doomsday into a caern, and you will believe a werewolf can fly. To the moon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, in speed, endurance, and strength, they're on a whole other level. Even if you can puncture endurance (which it's debatable - I remember a she-wolf hurting Supergilrl in a comic book, and surely our Werewolves ain't less sharp, but at the same time I grant you that OTHER times Supergilrl managed to tank magical attacks of a very high potency. Comic books are very contradictory), you still have to contend with the other two.<br /> <br /> Best way for splats to win would be to approach the problem lateraly. For instance, the hermetic seal that can throw you outside time and space (essentially freezing you in time and moving you outside space, to a pocket dimension of sorts), seems like it can work against most - it doesn't matter how strong or fast you are, you can't escape without a degree of reality warping (of the kind that, granted, superman has shown sometimes - but not in all versions). This to give an example, splats have lots of similar capabilities (and mages are particularly good at this).<br /> Also superheros tend to have decent mental/spiritual defneses, but I would argue that barring superman, gods, and psychic types, these aren't so overwhelming as their physical superiority - most of the time they're based on their great will and mental endurance and little more, hence a powerful Elder or equivalent should be able to dominate or use illusion to force some superheros to kill each other, don't you think?.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to suggest Paladin be a HIGH Willpower Formori. All the Bane really cares about is the rage and killing and torture the fact that Paladin is doing &quot;good' with it should give the players some food for thought on the Triat without having to go crossover heavy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since he was working for Pentex, you have an easy time justifying him being one- also it would give the guy even more reasons to hate that particular megacorporation the most. As long as he can keep some degree of control over his soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T08:03:22-08:00","id":1175174,"title":"","content":"Him being a formori, or at least close to being one sounds good. Once Paladin dies or is otherwise taken care of, those other vigilanties start to hit tbe streets. One idea i have is to have one of the heroes actually be either a Nuwisha or Corax hanging with a group of them in homid form. Can i have any suggestions why a Corax or Nuwisha would hang around costumed vigilanties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T10:55:58-08:00","id":1175224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175144#post1175144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most of the time they're based on their great will and mental endurance and little more, hence a powerful Elder or equivalent should be able to dominate or use illusion to force some superheros to kill each other, don't you think?.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends. Are other telepaths there? Martian Manhunter? Emma Frost? Jean Grey? Cable?<br /> <br /> Street level superheroes would certainly work. Wolverine, Spidey, Batman, etc would be awesome in a WoD game. As would Iron Man in a Technocracy game. <br /> <br /> Marvel heroes for the most part work well with the WoD. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-11-2018, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T11:00:51-08:00","id":1175225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175174#post1175174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i have any suggestions why a Corax or Nuwisha would hang around costumed vigilanties?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, because its hilarious? A Nuwisha might easily stick around for the lulz, maybe trying to lead the would-be caped crusaders against enemies of Gaia. Or not, whatever.<br /> <br /> There is also a possibility that Paladin's fomori status has aroused suspicion among a watchful Corax, who is keeping close tabs on the deceased hero's following.<br /> <br /> Addendum: no offense lads, but fictional character dick-measuring is kind of meaningless and tiresome and not particularly relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T12:15:12-08:00","id":1175250,"title":"","content":"I can also see a Nuwisha using her gifts to mess with crooks and with her own companions. That is, if a Nuwisha would participate in thrashing crooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T14:13:40-08:00","id":1175279,"title":"","content":"Well maybe not a traditional Corax.. BUT in Japanese Myth and incorporated into the WOD Tengu often take and train warriors/demon hunters to fight the monster of the world adapting an ancient tradition to a modern view of it.. could work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T20:40:24-08:00","id":1175356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175279#post1175279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well maybe not a traditional Corax.. BUT in Japanese Myth and incorporated into the WOD Tengu often take and train warriors/demon hunters to fight the monster of the world adapting an ancient tradition to a modern view of it.. could work?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Tengu training a couple of Paladin's internet followers into being Goblin Hunters could work. But, i wonder how i could justify a Hengenyokai traveling all the way to New Orleans?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T20:59:39-08:00","id":1175359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175356#post1175356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Tengu training a couple of Paladin's internet followers into being Goblin Hunters could work. But, i wonder how i could justify a Hengenyokai traveling all the way to New Orleans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplest answer: they were born there. It's a pretty cosmopolitan place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T22:13:23-08:00","id":1175376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175356#post1175356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Tengu training a couple of Paladin's internet followers into being Goblin Hunters could work. But, i wonder how i could justify a Hengenyokai traveling all the way to New Orleans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tengu have as much chance of Getting there as any Non Pure Ones Garou Tribe. Hell he could start talking to them on the internet and decide to train them as Goblin Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T22:30:13-08:00","id":1175377,"title":"","content":"Yeah, him just traveling there can work. I imagine the whole trained to kill Bakemonos could help if they encounter Fomori. I am also picturing a moment where two of these &quot;superheroes&quot; corner a hulking crook in a alleyway wearing a trenchcoat and hat, only for them to realize that the crook is actually a formori who says something along the lines of,&quot; You think I'm scared of a buncha punks wearing tights. Bring it on wimps, i will make sure to make your bodies identifiable for yer mommies.&quot; I am also wondering how PENTEX would react to this whole situation, considering that the founder of this movement was a former employee was a grudge against Magadon who ends up dying in one of their facilities either due to werewolves, A First Team or him blowing himself up along with the facility?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T13:36:47-08:00","id":1175833,"title":"","content":"In W20's source book on the Umbra the Wyld has a selection of Spirits including Superhero! These spirits manifest beyond the Gauntlet if the cry of justice or that of a child is strong enough to reach them on the other side. This idea of a wyld spirit confused me since most wyld spirits are strange and raw creationish, so its possible a spirit of a Superhero either use the vigilantes to feed its need for heroes and might imbue or look out for them. Possibly gaining a psuedo totem bond of sorts if these Vigilantes work as a unit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T17:44:19-08:00","id":1175875,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestion, Derp. I bet seeing a Wyld spirit hanging around a bunch of these &quot; caped crusaders&quot; would make quite a few Garou confused, especially the ones that revere the Wyld. I wonder what kind of Weaver spirit would hang around these superheroes? Also, besides Nuwisha and Corax, I wonder which other breed of Fera would take interest in these vigilantes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T19:34:03-08:00","id":1175893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175875#post1175875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the suggestion, Derp. I bet seeing a Wyld spirit hanging around a bunch of these &quot; caped crusaders&quot; would make quite a few Garou confused, especially the ones that revere the Wyld. I wonder what kind of Weaver spirit would hang around these superheroes? Also, besides Nuwisha and Corax, I wonder which other breed of Fera would take interest in these vigilantes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only changers that really revere the Wyld are the Ratkin, and I'd imagine that Munchmausen would find them quite... inspiring.<br /> <br /> As for Weaver equivalents, consider the various ideological splits that happen in comics, such as in the Civil War storyline regarding the superhero registration program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T20:30:31-08:00","id":1175903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175893#post1175893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only changers that really revere the Wyld are the Ratkin, and I'd imagine that Munchmausen would find them quite... inspiring.<br /> <br /> As for Weaver equivalents, consider the various ideological splits that happen in comics, such as in the Civil War storyline regarding the superhero registration program.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Munchmausen are insane, much like the rest of the Freak Aspects. It might get awkward when one of his more sane companions sees him interacting with a guy in a superhero costume. I wonder how a interaction between a Swashbuckler and one of these vigilanties would go? I do like the idea of two groups of &quot;heroes&quot;, one having the patronage of a Weaver spirit, the other of a wyld spirit, fighting each other while fighting crooks as well. With the rest of the changeling breeds, The Rokea, of course, would ignore them, same with the Nagah. I can see a lone Anansi wanting to use some of them for her own ends. Not sure about the Gurahl, Bastets and Kitsunes,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T20:38:51-08:00","id":1175905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175903#post1175903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Munchmausen are insane, much like the rest of the Freak Aspects. It might get awkward when one of his more sane companions sees him interacting with a guy in a superhero costume. I wonder how a interaction between a Swashbuckler and one of these vigilanties would go? I do like the idea of two groups of &quot;heroes&quot;, one having the patronage of a Weaver spirit, the other of a wyld spirit, fighting each other while fighting crooks as well. With the rest of the changeling breeds, The Rokea, of course, would ignore them, same with the Nagah. I can see a lone Anansi wanting to use some of them for her own ends. Not sure about the Gurahl, Bastets and Kitsunes,</div> </div> </div> </div>Munchmausen are under no obligation to be only swashbucklers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-13T23:36:33-08:00","id":1175922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175903#post1175903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Munchmausen are insane, much like the rest of the Freak Aspects. It might get awkward when one of his more sane companions sees him interacting with a guy in a superhero costume. I wonder how a interaction between a Swashbuckler and one of these vigilanties would go? I do like the idea of two groups of &quot;heroes&quot;, one having the patronage of a Weaver spirit, the other of a wyld spirit, fighting each other while fighting crooks as well. With the rest of the changeling breeds, The Rokea, of course, would ignore them, same with the Nagah. I can see a lone Anansi wanting to use some of them for her own ends. Not sure about the Gurahl, Bastets and Kitsunes,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of the Munmausen I've seen in play: A &quot;magical Girl&quot;, full pulp hero(bakced up with an engineer pack mate), &quot;The worlds Greatest Detective&quot; Munmausen are.. somewhere on the edge of Malkavian and Marauder. They don't full on have reality in on their shit.. but it gets close.<br /> <br /> As for Fera well how populated and focused on the heroes should your game be? IF the Central focus is a couple of spirit cults that end up looking like Low grade super heroes its an option. If you want a Tengu to abuse the situation that's an option but I think the important thing you need to ask yourself is how much of the plot is going to be around mortals dressing up in costumes.<br /> <br /> Because player Fera aren't going to have a huge problem &quot;Fixing&quot; this with either violence or judicious use of Gifts. They also wouldn't have problems tearing through the Criminal underworld asside from the fact that for the most part that's backed by someone(vampires, Mages, werewolves... etc)<br /> <br /> Or the players can take &quot;Thor&quot; as Totem for a Pack/Sentai and just go all in and you can do werewolf the comic. Its going to be more batman than superman but still its not an invalid take either. Either way I feel like as this thread has gone on its drifted from &quot;neat side character' (the Paladin) to the sole focus of your Chronicle. If your Chronicle is going to be about various degrees of people dressing up in wierd costumes and punching people you may want to consider it from that perspective. Take some of the tropes and mix them liberally wiht the world of Darkness<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T00:34:10-08:00","id":1175935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175922#post1175922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Of the Munmausen I've seen in play: A &quot;magical Girl&quot;, full pulp hero(bakced up with an engineer pack mate), &quot;The worlds Greatest Detective&quot; Munmausen are.. somewhere on the edge of Malkavian and Marauder. They don't full on have reality in on their shit.. but it gets close.<br /> <br /> As for Fera well how populated and focused on the heroes should your game be? IF the Central focus is a couple of spirit cults that end up looking like Low grade super heroes its an option. If you want a Tengu to abuse the situation that's an option but I think the important thing you need to ask yourself is how much of the plot is going to be around mortals dressing up in costumes.<br /> <br /> Because player Fera aren't going to have a huge problem &quot;Fixing&quot; this with either violence or judicious use of Gifts. They also wouldn't have problems tearing through the Criminal underworld asside from the fact that for the most part that's backed by someone(vampires, Mages, werewolves... etc)<br /> <br /> Or the players can take &quot;Thor&quot; as Totem for a Pack/Sentai and just go all in and you can do werewolf the comic. Its going to be more batman than superman but still its not an invalid take either. Either way I feel like as this thread has gone on its drifted from &quot;neat side character' (the Paladin) to the sole focus of your Chronicle. If your Chronicle is going to be about various degrees of people dressing up in wierd costumes and punching people you may want to consider it from that perspective. Take some of the tropes and mix them liberally wiht the world of Darkness<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thor is no totem to take, as the Get of Fenris will attest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T06:26:06-08:00","id":1175963,"title":"","content":"No, the campaign is not centered around these heroes, though some of them do become major characters and othets cause situations like pissing off the local BSDs. I was just trying to develop how the Werewolf setting would react to these vigilanties. But, since i am doing a Garou game, i should be thinking about how the 13 tribes would react to them, not the other Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:15:40-08:00","id":1176172,"title":"","content":"A thought just popped into my head. I wonder how Wyld tainted vigilanties would act when compared to Weaver tainted ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:23:00-08:00","id":1176174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175935#post1175935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thor is no totem to take, as the Get of Fenris will attest!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Get of Fenris believe alot of things! But I meant that more as a generic &quot;Totem manifests as a Superhero&quot; for example (Captain) American Dream, or Spider(man), New World Trinity, The Monkey King, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:38:54-08:00","id":1176179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176174#post1176174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Get of Fenris believe alot of things! But I meant that more as a generic &quot;Totem manifests as a Superhero&quot; for example (Captain) American Dream, or Spider(man), New World Trinity, The Monkey King, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't about belief. They shed blood against the Aesir. The Aesir are enemies of Gaia, and other groups aren't exactly leaping up to defend them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:45:24-08:00","id":1176183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1175963#post1175963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the campaign is not centered around these heroes, though some of them do become major characters and othets cause situations like pissing off the local BSDs. I was just trying to develop how the Werewolf setting would react to these vigilanties. But, since i am doing a Garou game, i should be thinking about how the 13 tribes would react to them, not the other Fera.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly people being crazy on the street corner in the world of darkness can both be both &quot;that person is crazy&quot; or &quot;This is part of a world spanning supernatural conspiracy that dates before the dawn of time&quot; and all manner of degrees inbetween. So people dressing up in costumes and beating up criminals has all sorts of possibilities.<br /> <br /> 1. Is it just people being crazy? Is this just abit of colorful flavor you've thrown into the background of a larger game? Its a legitimate option. You start with the Paladin as the only super powered one, and then have the players deal with how they feel about this mortal who was able to force the wyrm to do &quot;good&quot; in his game of revenge.. and whether they should protect these others from theirown potential stupidity.<br /> <br /> 2. Is it part of a Fera legacy being hidden in modern guise? Then you get a story about them bringing in a potential ally and overcoming cultural differences. Also a fun bit of story.<br /> <br /> 3. Is it local Umbral shenanigans? A couple of spirits with the right charms start directing people along.. its wyld at first then some weaver(CONTROL) should the Garou care? Should they be concerned before some urge wyrm picks up on the idea? should they be concerned that this could corrupt things.. and what happens when a Gaian spirit gets involved?<br /> <br /> 4. Cosmic Umbral Shenanigans. We are seeing the effects of the super hero start to bloom readily in the Umbra and its effecting the real world. NEw potential allies are growing all around.. and new potential foes. Totems are taking new faces and making odd requests.. but such is the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Nothing says you can't use different degrees of the idea just that you probably should focus on what you want to do with them rather than some &quot;well how would things react&quot; because.. it varies it really does. It varies from &quot;not give a shit&quot; to &quot;part of a cosmic transformation of the symbols of heroism&quot; and thus you have alot of leeway with what you want to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:48:53-08:00","id":1176185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176179#post1176179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't about belief. They shed blood against the Aesir. The Aesir are enemies of Gaia, and other groups aren't exactly leaping up to defend them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thor the Aesir is a man with a beard and red hair... Thor the Asgardian talks like a bad shakespearean character has blonde hair, acts generally differently was turned into a frog...<br /> <br /> That is to say there's enough difference between whatever the Get fought and whatever is formed by Marvel, there's definately enough difference between Typhon the Totem and Typhon the vampire...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:51:44-08:00","id":1176186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176185#post1176185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thor the Aesir is a man with a beard and red hair... Thor the Asgardian talks like a bad shakespearean character has blonde hair, acts generally differently was turned into a frog...<br /> <br /> That is to say there's enough difference between whatever the Get fought and whatever is formed by Marvel, there's definately enough difference between Typhon the Totem and Typhon the vampire...</div> </div> </div> </div>Typhon was only ever an alias for a vampire. Also, you forgot about Typhon the Wani, possibly another different spirit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T22:58:34-08:00","id":1176194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176186#post1176186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Typhon was only ever an alias for a vampire. Also, you forgot about Typhon the Wani, possibly another different spirit!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> New spirits come into being(or old spirits take on new faces) with a certain amount of regularity in the Modern world. The American Dream, City Parents, All Mighty Dollar, or Easy Credit. Or worst of all lets look at General Lee. General Lee is a totem that is entirely based upon a car from Dukes of Hazzard.<br /> <br /> I would say &quot;Marvel Thor&quot; hits at least the level of General Lee. Now the Get being upset and attacking you would be an option and a Reasonable one, and I would in no way expect a Get to take said potential spirit, but if you want to run a game about taking a relatively new spirit empowering it as a totem and growing with it as it grows in power Its an option. THis could just as readily be &quot;The man of Iron&quot; as a totem or &quot;the Dark Knight&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T18:11:35-08:00","id":1176429,"title":"","content":"Iron Man as a spirit totem, I wonder what that would look like? Also, i like options number 1,3,4 the best. I can definatley see these vigilanties effecting the whole Umbra sooner or later, providing they manage to spread from North America into a different continent, probably either Europe or Asia. Also, i don't remember their being a Spider totem, unless you are referring to Ananasa or one of those spider like spirits that weave the pattern web. I wonder how awkward that would be for a Ananasi to have to keep an eye on a bunch of costumed vigilanties because her Queen took an interest in them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-15-2018, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T10:42:45-08:00","id":1176544,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts:<br /> <br /> There was a thread on the (ancient) alt.games.white-wolf newsgroup presenting several of the Avengers as inspiration for a Technocracy amalgam. Tony Stark as Iteration X, Steve Rogers as a Progenitor, Janet van Dyne with the Syndicate, and so forth. It was fun. <br /> <br /> I think &quot;superheroes&quot; works best in the World of Darkness when kept at a fairly moderate level, the sort of thing from some of the pulps and their predecessors, some of the very early comics, and the Bronze Age's revival of the &quot;street level&quot; and &quot;international agent&quot; genres (which happened to coincide with a similar resurgence of pulp style adventure novels). More of a sort of &quot;things in the shadows&quot; and &quot;urban legends&quot; angle, that sometimes drifts into the public view. Marvel's Netflix series do a good job of this, I think, especially the first season of Daredevil. Likewise The Shadow and The Phantom (I really wish there were better movie versions of both), as well as the Rocketeer. Philip Wylie's The Gladiator is another good one. The Destroyer novels, as well as some of the other long running book series from the 70s and 80s. Also, The Strange Talent of Luther Strode, a pretty good (and rather violent) comic book series. And the movie Dark Man, an underrated gem from the 90s. <br /> <br /> If one goes the full supernatural route, I think &quot;vampire as superhero&quot; works best with Nosferatu (the masked avenger who clouds men's minds with Obfuscate) and Caitiff (the introvert who becomes a vampire and decides to become a dark anti-hero). With werewolves, a Garou is essentially &quot;what if Conan the Barbarian walked the earth today&quot;, and &quot;Masked Vigilante&quot; probably works pretty good as a concept for Glasswalkers or Bone Gnawers, and maybe a few others (say, a Silver Fang with more than a few screws loose who decides being rich and powerful means they should go the full Batman/Green Hornet). The Akashic Brotherhood and Sons of Ether work best for Mages, I think. And you could probably have a lot of fun with a Changeling oath circle who try to be heroes. I guess if you wanted to get really weird, you could have a gang of wraiths who possess people and have them act as superheroes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T10:58:43-08:00","id":1176548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176544#post1176544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thoughts:<br /> <br /> There was a thread on the (ancient) alt.games.white-wolf newsgroup presenting several of the Avengers as inspiration for a Technocracy amalgam. Tony Stark as Iteration X, Steve Rogers as a Progenitor, Janet van Dyne with the Syndicate, and so forth. It was fun.<br /> <br /> a Garou is essentially &quot;what if Conan the Barbarian walked the earth today&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>I like all of those. I get a lot of inspiration for Garou(and Changing Breeds) from Thor, Sub Mariner, etc. <br /> <br /> Especially stuff from the 80's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T12:18:26-08:00","id":1176565,"title":"","content":"There actually is a pre-made character template in the revised Lasombra book that is supposed to be a quasi-deranged modern version of The Shadow, but for some reason I think the original art notes of &quot;wearing a slouch hat&quot; got interpreted as &quot;wearing a slouched (baseball) hat&quot;. So the end result looks kind of mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T14:58:04-08:00","id":1176612,"title":"","content":"I also think there was a template in Nosferatu revised that was sorta like a Nossie version of the Punisher.<br /> <br /> Dark Crusader I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T18:09:12-08:00","id":1176644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176612#post1176612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think there was a template in Nosferatu revised that was sorta like a Nossie version of the Punisher.<br /> <br /> Dark Crusader I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you are correct. That as a fun one. The two would make for part of a weirdly interesting coterie. (Sort of the same way the Assamite Black Hand tactical officer and the Ravnos psi ops agent would, or the 1st ed Brujah Fake Rapper and Toreador Comic Book Celebrity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T20:53:05-08:00","id":1176684,"title":"","content":"Good ideas so far guys. I wonder if the Camerilla and the Anarchs would view these costumed vigilanties as a possible Masqurade breach? I am also wonder how the Technocrats would handle them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T03:12:12-08:00","id":1176734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176684#post1176684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good ideas so far guys. I wonder if the Camerilla and the Anarchs would view these costumed vigilanties as a possible Masqurade breach? I am also wonder how the Technocrat