ote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176876#post1176876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points on the Technocrats and Camerilla. I can just picture a Proginator making a Captain America-style hero to test a new steroid. Also, i am thinking that the only clan of vampires that would hate these &quot;heroes&quot; in general would be the Giovonnis. I wonder how the Camerilla and Sabbat would interact with these heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you've seen Jessica Jones, the Cop from that is what I'd imagine the Progenitors getting &quot;involved&quot; would look like.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Giovanni are.. well weird. There are those tied up in organized crime but its their family organized crime if these heroes are going after the other organizations against them well maybe little whisper from a ghost here or there?<br /> <br /> On the Camarilla, a particular Camarilla vampire is likely to have some sort of inroads in various criminal organizations. Its just useful especially when the Camarilla will broadly have a solid hold over mortal society in general. There will be things completely outside it but generally speaking they will have something in various spheres of influence.<br /> <br /> That being said, unless there's a sabbat seige or the Werewolves are particularly active in the are the Camarilla vampires will be at eachothers throats trying to jockey for power and undercut each other's bases. So the &quot;heroes&quot; are likely to both be a problem for Certain Camarilla vampires but also a tool for others. This might be a split along clan lines(ventrue vs Brujah) or cotorie based etc. Of course the Masquerade will be Key and someone might get blamed for using such &quot;flamboyant&quot; methods.<br /> <br /> Like all vampires humans broadly function into three categories for Sabbat, Food, Tools, future vampire. Unlike other groups they have some unique uses. The heroes are going to be stepping on someone's toes so using them subtly by pumping them into ghouls and sending them in without much knowledge as part an opening strike against the cam(or potentially rivals since as much as &quot;We don't do mortal things&quot; they try to say they do.) Now if the city is Cam they can push it up to the next and most hilarious level of &quot;Hey wouldn't it be fucking hilarious to build a shovel head pack full of superheroes&quot;. Sabbat might include hunting them while dressed up in costumes or doing Joker cosplay as some sort of Game of instinct. And finally of course there's the obvious of &quot;hey these people are a cut above your average mortal fuckers.. Embrace as true sabbat&quot;<br /> <br /> Though Honestly if we want to REALLY crazy crossover.. changeling is Right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:47:49-08:00","id":1177342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177204#post1177204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you've seen Jessica Jones, the Cop from that is what I'd imagine the Progenitors getting &quot;involved&quot; would look like.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Giovanni are.. well weird. There are those tied up in organized crime but its their family organized crime if these heroes are going after the other organizations against them well maybe little whisper from a ghost here or there?<br /> <br /> On the Camarilla, a particular Camarilla vampire is likely to have some sort of inroads in various criminal organizations. Its just useful especially when the Camarilla will broadly have a solid hold over mortal society in general. There will be things completely outside it but generally speaking they will have something in various spheres of influence.<br /> <br /> That being said, unless there's a sabbat seige or the Werewolves are particularly active in the are the Camarilla vampires will be at eachothers throats trying to jockey for power and undercut each other's bases. So the &quot;heroes&quot; are likely to both be a problem for Certain Camarilla vampires but also a tool for others. This might be a split along clan lines(ventrue vs Brujah) or cotorie based etc. Of course the Masquerade will be Key and someone might get blamed for using such &quot;flamboyant&quot; methods.<br /> <br /> Like all vampires humans broadly function into three categories for Sabbat, Food, Tools, future vampire. Unlike other groups they have some unique uses. The heroes are going to be stepping on someone's toes so using them subtly by pumping them into ghouls and sending them in without much knowledge as part an opening strike against the cam(or potentially rivals since as much as &quot;We don't do mortal things&quot; they try to say they do.) Now if the city is Cam they can push it up to the next and most hilarious level of &quot;Hey wouldn't it be fucking hilarious to build a shovel head pack full of superheroes&quot;. Sabbat might include hunting them while dressed up in costumes or doing Joker cosplay as some sort of Game of instinct. And finally of course there's the obvious of &quot;hey these people are a cut above your average mortal fuckers.. Embrace as true sabbat&quot;<br /> <br /> Though Honestly if we want to REALLY crazy crossover.. changeling is Right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou know, Changelings hanging with these superheroes makes since. Because, no doubt these guys would be generating glamour by making superheroes a real thing. Whether the type of glamour they generate is a good thing or bad thing I guess depends on the Changeling. The only real kith I can see actually doing the superhero thing would be the Trolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-19-2018, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:17:21-08:00","id":1177383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177204#post1177204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you've seen Jessica Jones, the Cop from that is what I'd imagine the Progenitors getting &quot;involved&quot; would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nuke is more Pentex-like, IMO.<br /> <br /> Now give me a red.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:55:16-08:00","id":1177393,"title":"","content":"A Pentex created superhero. That has bad news written all over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T14:19:19-08:00","id":1177415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177077#post1177077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thor was his own jerkish counterpart before his redemption arc, really. Also, the aforementioned characters could all end up grouping together anyway, assuming that you made a Thor clone (far from unheard of in comic books, evil clones).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Thor gets banished to Midgard and falls in with a bunch of meth and gun dealing bikers ....<br /> <br /> And yes, Nuke is one of my go-tos for examples of how PENTEX's less ridiculous efforts with Project Odyssey should look (along side the original Universal Soldier, DC's Bane, and the Juicers from the RIFTS RPG).<br /> <br /> (My example for total balls-to-the-wall over-the-top ridiculousness with Project Odyssey is the scrapped Jurassic Park IV script involving <a href=\"https://io9.gizmodo.com/5950364/scrapped-concept-art-from-jurassic-park-4-shows-off-insane-dinosaur-commandos\" target=\"_blank\">mutant dinosaur commandos.</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-19-2018, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:48:08-08:00","id":1177464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177415#post1177415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. Thor gets banished to Midgard and falls in with a bunch of meth and gun dealing bikers ....<br /> <br /> And yes, Nuke is one of my go-tos for examples of how PENTEX's less ridiculous efforts with Project Odyssey should look (along side the original Universal Soldier, DC's Bane, and the Juicers from the RIFTS RPG).<br /> <br /> (My example for total balls-to-the-wall over-the-top ridiculousness with Project Odyssey is the scrapped Jurassic Park IV script involving <a href=\"https://io9.gizmodo.com/5950364/scrapped-concept-art-from-jurassic-park-4-shows-off-insane-dinosaur-commandos\" target=\"_blank\">mutant dinosaur commandos.</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Odyssey concentrates on psychic powers. You're be looking for Illiad, or possibly Aeneid fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T20:19:54-08:00","id":1177503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177464#post1177464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Odyssey concentrates on psychic powers. You're be looking for Illiad, or possibly Aeneid fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bleh, yes. I constantly get those two backwards (and have done so consistantly for twenty years now). Probably the main reason I dislike the names so much. (I'd have gone with Gilgamesh and Cassandra or something.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T22:19:01-08:00","id":1177523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177342#post1177342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYou know, Changelings hanging with these superheroes makes since. Because, no doubt these guys would be generating glamour by making superheroes a real thing. Whether the type of glamour they generate is a good thing or bad thing I guess depends on the Changeling. The only real kith I can see actually doing the superhero thing would be the Trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changelings get all sorts of stuff for Following their Oaths, and Revenge is practically a Seelie virtue, so Trolls are a good option but honestly I can see any Kith might work.<br /> <br /> Lets Take your Paladin for example. He had a particularly banal life so he never had an option for Crystalis. But the loss of his family full Punisher style shatters his banal little world and gives him the chance to remember his fairy soul. He's an Autumn Sidhe and always had been! How dare this world do this to him? How dare this world be like this! HE WILL MAKE THEM PAY! Suddenly he's building up a gathering of dreamers/retinue of enchanted bent to his will. He ravages criminals into madness where he can, and murders when he doesn't. He is grand and glorious.. awesome in the old testament way.. Terrific in that he inspires terror..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T22:23:15-08:00","id":1177524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177383#post1177383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nuke is more Pentex-like, IMO.<br /> <br /> Now give me a red.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Progenitors have a whole division built around Drugs that make you better, Reason why I think TV nuke is more Progenitor... Comic nuke is definately more formori. But if we want to look at really frightening visuals I'm just going to compare Captain America's technological coocoon to the methods used in Bakemono Rite...<br /> <br /> Purple Man is more what I'd treat as a Formori","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T07:10:07-08:00","id":1177579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177524#post1177524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Progenitors have a whole division built around Drugs that make you better, Reason why I think TV nuke is more Progenitor... Comic nuke is definately more formori</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I can agree with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T11:48:04-08:00","id":1177652,"title":"","content":"The Sidhe knight version of Paladin sounds great. Now i wonder what a Eshu superhero and a Boggin Superhero would be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T20:53:43-08:00","id":1177765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177652#post1177652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidhe knight version of Paladin sounds great. Now i wonder what a Eshu superhero and a Boggin Superhero would be like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eshu might be a bit less likely to stay, they are more 70s Green lantern/Green arrow traveling the country getting into adventures. They show up have crazy chaos and eventually move along. Or they are the worldly mentor who teaches the brash young guy how all about being awesome with stories from through out the world.<br /> <br /> The Boggan is the guy everyone depends upon. He's very much a ensemble cast Superhero type vs Has hisown book but he's a KEY part of that book. He's not only the reason why you aren't running around half naked in bloody rags, but the reason you have food and medical care between runs. He provides, he makes the little bits meet. It may not be as focused but someone has to keep everything running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T09:41:42-08:00","id":1177869,"title":"","content":"Eshu would be the wandering adventurer type, be it the small scale North American type of 60s. 70s and 80s TV (Have Gun Will Travel, Kung Fu, The Incredible Hulk, Knight Rider, The Master, The A-Team) or the more globe-trotting style of international agents of intrigue (James Bond, Modesty Blaise, Nemesis, Manhunter).<br /> <br /> Boggin would be the sidekick, essentially a modern version of Sam from Lord of the Rings by way of Alfred from Batman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T17:59:45-08:00","id":1177974,"title":"","content":"I can see a Boggin being a Alfred-type of character.<br /> \u200bA Pooka superhero would probably be a Spider-Man-type, using his shapeshifting powers and tricks to fight crooks while annoying them with quips and jokes about their intelligence, weight, etc.<br /> \u200bA Selkie would use her powers to turn into her seal form and spy on crooks then report her findings to the rest of the motley. Not sure how they could help during the actual fight against the crooks.<br /> Trolls are self-explanatory. A stoic figure with a sense of justice would make a great bruiser.<br /> \u200bNot sure how Piskies and Satyrs could be good superhero's though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:36:41-08:00","id":1178085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177974#post1177974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see a Boggin being a Alfred-type of character.<br /> \u200bA Pooka superhero would probably be a Spider-Man-type, using his shapeshifting powers and tricks to fight crooks while annoying them with quips and jokes about their intelligence, weight, etc.<br /> \u200bA Selkie would use her powers to turn into her seal form and spy on crooks then report her findings to the rest of the motley. Not sure how they could help during the actual fight against the crooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cantrips.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trolls are self-explanatory. A stoic figure with a sense of justice would make a great bruiser.<br /> \u200bNot sure how Piskies and Satyrs could be good superhero's though. </div> </div> </div>Antman and the Goat-Flash. Some cantrips may be necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:40:34-08:00","id":1178103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1177974#post1177974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see a Boggin being a Alfred-type of character.<br /> \u200bA Pooka superhero would probably be a Spider-Man-type, using his shapeshifting powers and tricks to fight crooks while annoying them with quips and jokes about their intelligence, weight, etc.<br /> \u200bA Selkie would use her powers to turn into her seal form and spy on crooks then report her findings to the rest of the motley. Not sure how they could help during the actual fight against the crooks.<br /> Trolls are self-explanatory. A stoic figure with a sense of justice would make a great bruiser.<br /> \u200bNot sure how Piskies and Satyrs could be good superhero's though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings are perhaps the least bound to their splats.. especially post c20. In Revised there were &quot;secret&quot; kith only arts but in c20 anyone can use anything, some are better at certain realms but everyone can use everything. The advantage of being a motley is you can all focus on One art and since its a 2 point dip into fae to share its less &quot;I have this power&quot; and its more &quot;I buff everyone with this&quot; &quot;and I buff everyone with this&quot;...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T20:09:14-08:00","id":1178319,"title":"","content":"Good point with the cantrips being used liberally. Now the only kith i didn't mention besides the Irish one is the Arcadian Sidhe. I highly doubt a Seelie noble would really come out of his freehold to beat the stuffing out of petty thugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T21:53:06-08:00","id":1178351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1178319#post1178319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point with the cantrips being used liberally. Now the only kith i didn't mention besides the Irish one is the Arcadian Sidhe. I highly doubt a Seelie noble would really come out of his freehold to beat the stuffing out of petty thugs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never Forget a Debt. Plus Arcadian Sidhe do have human memories, and many replace the child's soul at birth. I could EASILY justify a Arcadian Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T11:43:51-08:00","id":1178497,"title":"","content":"House Dougal as the stoic technical expert (sort of a clockwork/steampunk/dieselpunk take on the likes of the Rocketeer, Steel, or even Oracle; see also characters like Dame Progress, The Assemblyman, Mock Turtle, and the Junkman from Astro City). <br /> <br /> House Eiluned as the secretive and mysterious operator in the shadows (Black Widow, Nemesis, Shroud) or mystical specialist (Madam Xanadu, Hellstorm).<br /> <br /> House Fiona as the dashing and romantic modern day swashbuckler (Green Arrow back in the early days, Astro City's Crackerjack)<br /> <br /> House Gwydion as the super-serious and overly idealistic modern day crusader against dishonor and falsehood (I don't really have an example for this off the top of my head).<br /> <br /> House Liam as the protector of the helpless and downtrodden (Cloak and Dagger, Demolition Man, the Netflix version of Luke Cage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T21:35:20-08:00","id":1178670,"title":"","content":"House Scathach:&quot;I.. AM THE NIGHT! seriously the Children of the Queen of the Land of Shadows are pretty much built to be the Stealthy avenger.<br /> <br /> Beaumayn: are abit more focused around fighting the monsters of the dreaming than the mortals.<br /> <br /> Ailil: Arrogant through and through incapable of seeing their failures. Still sometimes they are just as good as they think they are masters of politics and social interaction<br /> <br /> Balor: I AM THE LAW! Every Superhero as a statement on authoritarianism is Credo of House Balor. Judge Dredd, certain interpretations of the Punisher...<br /> <br /> Varich: are focused on patterns and riddles, the times the Riddler has been Redeemed, L from Death note these are the types of Varich Heroes you'd see.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have a hard time with the other Unseelie houses if anyone wants to try them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T10:35:51-08:00","id":1178860,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input on the Sidhe Houses. I am picturing at least one of these Changeling heroes temporaily Enchanting crooks so they can use their full Fae arsenal to fight them without having to rely on subtle cantrips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T15:14:02-08:00","id":1178964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1178860#post1178860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the input on the Sidhe Houses. I am picturing at least one of these Changeling heroes temporaily Enchanting crooks so they can use their full Fae arsenal to fight them without having to rely on subtle cantrips.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changelings can Call upon the Wyrd to pull out their full powers. They also have something called the Enchanting Blow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:20:04-08:00","id":1179396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1178964#post1178964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Changelings can Call upon the Wyrd to pull out their full powers. They also have something called the Enchanting Blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the image the of a thug suddenly being greeted by a giant blue fist, courtesy of a troll who used Enchanting Blow on him. Also, if you don't mind me going back to Werewolf for a second, what do you think a Drone superhero and a Gorgon superhero would be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T21:54:15-08:00","id":1179437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179396#post1179396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the image the of a thug suddenly being greeted by a giant blue fist, courtesy of a troll who used Enchanting Blow on him. Also, if you don't mind me going back to Werewolf for a second, what do you think a Drone superhero and a Gorgon superhero would be like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they would have similar issues with needing to push the Human above the spirit. Drones wouldn't be flashy they would be subtle agents of stasis while we think of the Technocracy for the Souless MIB(and that is their standard) someone who just does one job and seems to have lost much of their humanity to the One song is the nature of Droning. Omac some of the Sentinels, something cold. Mechanical something that used to be human.<br /> <br /> By canon there are no human Gorgons, that being said I've never particularly liked that statement. That being said Gorgons are agents of CHAOS. While they might destroy a criminal syndicate they are going to leave alot of collateral damage. Its probably alot harder to keep these sorts of spirits happy with hitting &quot;the right targets' than the wyrm.<br /> <br /> Kami, well you didn't bring them up but might as well finish the cycle right? Kami wouldn't play so different than Fera though they are not necissarily creatures of Rage, of course you could also go in profoundly other directions and get things like Swamp Thing. Still Gaia is the least cruel and the merge of spirit and FLesh would have the least conflict so they might be the most &quot;humane&quot; of the Possessed.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Since we might as well get to it.. Wraith.<br /> <br /> Wraith has some really obvious parallels in comics, Dead-man who's really just a ghost who possesses people(easy) and various ressurected types(The Crow, Solmon Grundy..) these are pretty standardly covered with Risen.<br /> <br /> Of course your Ghost Hero has all sorts of reasons to hide is name and face to take up an alias as.. what he's doing is profoundly illegal.. on the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-26-2018, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T23:04:46-08:00","id":1179445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179437#post1179437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By canon there are no human Gorgons, that being said I've never particularly liked that statement. That being said Gorgons are agents of CHAOS. While they might destroy a criminal syndicate they are going to leave alot of collateral damage. Its probably alot harder to keep these sorts of spirits happy with hitting &quot;the right targets' than the wyrm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gorgons can usually be counted on to target Wyrm-creatures if it's within the purview of their tenant to do so, as they hate the forces trying to do them in. Anything after that, though, and it's about where you cut it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:00:47-08:00","id":1179564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179437#post1179437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By canon there are no human Gorgons, that being said I've never particularly liked that statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise. It always struck me as strangely limiting for a force of unbridled chaos, creativity and change. And, honestly, if you've ever seen the Brotherhood of Dada from Grant Morrison's 1980s run on Doom Patrol, your brain will pretty much <i>demand</i> that there be humans possessed by Wyld spirits. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:18:32-08:00","id":1179568,"title":"","content":"I made a malk who thinks he's a certain superhero. Uses his vast riches to increase the wealth gap and perpetuate more poverty and crime, so he can run about in a cape and beat the shit out of the poor people who killed his parents.<br /> <br /> that said, I'd go with a formori of narcissism or a mage experiment, maybe a psychic. An idiot with no special powers, maybe some skills, is always fair game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:22:12-08:00","id":1179569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1176194#post1176194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> New spirits come into being(or old spirits take on new faces) with a certain amount of regularity in the Modern world. The American Dream, City Parents, All Mighty Dollar, or Easy Credit.<b>Best of of all </b>lets look at General Lee. General Lee is a totem that is entirely based upon a car from <i>Dukes of Hazard</i>. <b>And that's awesome even if you don't care for <i>Dukes of Hazard. It's clearly the best totem, you should all look for excuses to take it.</i></b><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you don't mind me taking the liberty to fix your post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:20:55-08:00","id":1179635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179569#post1179569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you don't mind me taking the liberty to fix your post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I find the General Lee weird. If he has enough spiritual weight to be totem why wasn't Optimus Prime?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:28:21-08:00","id":1179641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179635#post1179635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I find the General Lee weird. If he has enough spiritual weight to be totem why wasn't Optimus Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of people really really love their cars, or their bikes, or anything else with a motor. Some would consider it a lifestyle. Now, I've only watched bits of dukes of hazard, or i don't remember it, but I think the spirit of -love of vehicles- would be a mighty one, and bone gnawers have an odd sense of humour, and &quot;general lee&quot; sounds like a flattering name for a car (which needs a name, because it's Your Specific Car that you love, that's how the spirit is i guess. Maybe there's the double meaning of &quot;general&quot; there too). My only gripe with the concept is that there isn't a similar named totem for a formation of motorcycles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T20:35:12-08:00","id":1179714,"title":"","content":"I love your input on Wraith superheroes. I especially think that Crow screams CWoD. Also, this video would pretty much sum up what a Akashtic Brother or a Kuei Jim would be like as a superhero. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ds_-Gbs88eI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ds_-Gbs88eI</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:06:46-08:00","id":1179723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179714#post1179714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love your input on Wraith superheroes. I especially think that Crow screams CWoD. Also, this video would pretty much sum up what a Akashtic Brother or a Kuei Jim would be like as a superhero. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ds_-Gbs88eI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ds_-Gbs88eI</a></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the sample characters for the werefoxes in Hengeyokai was straight-up a type of character played by Jackie Chan and had his likeness (a neighborhood protector, as in this very video), and Ling Chu, a weretiger based out of HK, is based on another type of character that he played (from Supercop, as Ling Chu is outright described as such in Bastet).<br /> <br /> (Gifts and regeneration can help cope for when those stunts don't go according to plan...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:34:44-08:00","id":1179730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179723#post1179723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the sample characters for the werefoxes in Hengeyokai was straight-up a type of character played by Jackie Chan and had his likeness (a neighborhood protector, as in this very video), and Ling Chu, a weretiger based out of HK, is based on another type of character that he played (from Supercop, as Ling Chu is outright described as such in Bastet).<br /> <br /> (Gifts and regeneration can help cope for when those stunts don't go according to plan...)</div> </div> </div> </div>A Kitsune superhero sounds badass, so does a Bastet one. Also, i am thinking that a few kinfolk would get involved with these vigilanties. Either to prove themselves useful to their families, being moles for the Fera, or to use them to strike against Pentex and other human servants of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-27-2018, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:38:33-08:00","id":1179733,"title":"","content":"KJ well you have a couple of ways to go.<br /> <br /> First there are the Kanbujian, those who rise outside proper channels and through shear force of will regain their sapience pushing their Po back. A Kanbujian who takes judicious use from various superhero genre to understand his situation(Hulk, Sentry, Etrigan..) really any &quot;deal with a monster&quot; powered type in the background could go this way. It might actually entertain the Po to have you dress up like a superhero.. or it might be a matter of control.<br /> <br /> Of &quot;proper&quot; KJ Masked Avengers DO have a tradition historically in the East. Its easy enough to pick a reason for the various Traditional Dharmas: Avenging the Dead(boneflowers) Punishing the wicked(Cranes, Devil Tigers), Because I'm a bad ass Monster who kicked his way out of Hell(actual character concept in Thrashing Dragons) Because I think I'm going to learn something from being batman(Thousand whispers). The heresies are abit trickier but I'd think the Phoenixes would have something interesting to learn playing the game of superhero and protector of the community, as might the Divine Tribe in their attempt to become gods. The Cerulean Veils with their focus on both types of spirits would be rather weird but I could see a very Grant Morrisonesque superhero narrative there.<br /> <br /> The Tempests i have no idea what to do with, but that's generally my issue with them. As for the Scorpion Eaters.. they'd make horrible heroes... but they would totally dress up like a Clown to just fuck with you. They litterally &quot;For the Lolz&quot; as an ideology, with twisted powers that make the world worse with each and every use.<br /> <br /> IF someone wants to talk about Mummies they've never been my Forte and they ahve some issue with globe hopping<br /> <br /> Hunters are well.. Hunters ARE superheroes. They have an origin, are driven to fight evil and generally have more of a &quot;secret identity&quot; than your average entity.<br /> <br /> Demons come into human bodies on the loss of the soul or a near death experience... and thus the human memories mitigate the suffering the demon proper has felt, this gives you a pretty easy access to them playing superhero either using human ideals to help deal with torment, protecting your Thralls(or empowering them.. go bat demon family!). They are however Extremely tangental to a Werewolf game since metawise they were developed as a concept long after Werewolf had its world view built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T22:10:01-08:00","id":1179741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179733#post1179733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blu