il and generally have more of a &amp;quot;secret identity&amp;quot; than your average entity.<br /> <br /> Demons come into human bodies on the loss of the soul or a near death experience... and thus the human memories mitigate the suffering the demon proper has felt, this gives you a pretty easy access to them playing superhero either using human ideals to help deal with torment, protecting your Thralls(or empowering them.. go bat demon family!). They are however Extremely tangental to a Werewolf game since metawise they were developed as a concept long after Werewolf had its world view built.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see some of the Imbued buddying up with these vigilanties. My only concern is that the Imbued are concerned with fighting monsters in the sgadows controlling humanity. Woyld some of them really take up beating the snot out of thugs while having to deal with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T22:33:01-08:00","id":1179747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179741#post1179741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see some of the Imbued buddying up with these vigilanties. My only concern is that the Imbued are concerned with fighting monsters in the sgadows controlling humanity. Woyld some of them really take up beating the snot out of thugs while having to deal with that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imbued are vigilantes. If you have the power and drive to &quot;Stop evil&quot; are you going to be &quot;Well that human trafficing ring is ok.. it doesn't have any vampires in it...&quot; That's before the fact that various degrees of crime DO function as covers for supernatural powerplays.<br /> <br /> Also the Imbued are generally the least knowledgeable about the greater organization of and might latch onto conflating Organized crime or particular groups with the supernatural. Or they might just be racist assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-27-2018, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T06:12:48-08:00","id":1179805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179747#post1179747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Imbued are vigilantes. If you have the power and drive to &quot;Stop evil&quot; are you going to be &quot;Well that human trafficing ring is ok.. it doesn't have any vampires in it...&quot; That's before the fact that various degrees of crime DO function as covers for supernatural powerplays.<br /> <br /> Also the Imbued are generally the least knowledgeable about the greater organization of and might latch onto conflating Organized crime or particular groups with the supernatural. Or they might just be racist assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGood point. I just figured since the Imbued mostly fought the Undead and other monsters human crooks would go underneath their notice. I guess the best types of imbued to don the cowl of a superhero would be Defenders, Judges and Avengers. Innocence's would be the worst type of Hunter to become a superhero, same with the Waywards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-27-2018, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T13:12:52-08:00","id":1179917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1179805#post1179805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bGood point. I just figured since the Imbued mostly fought the Undead and other monsters human crooks would go underneath their notice. I guess the best types of imbued to don the cowl of a superhero would be Defenders, Judges and Avengers. Innocence's would be the worst type of Hunter to become a superhero, same with the Waywards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Depends on the story you want to tell.. Waywards would be a Hell of a superhero.. they could even have a white skull on their chest...<br /> <br /> As for whether something is beneath the notice of a person, that is always up to the character in question, plenty of Fera would make the argument that human evils are beneath the notice of those who should be fighting the wyrm, plenty of vampires would say the same about how they should be really fighting other vampire group, Traditions vs Technocracy etc.. There always will be people saying you are wasting your time unless you are part of the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:08:16-08:00","id":1179949,"title":"","content":"I forget which book - maybe the Players Guide or one of the Creed books - brought up the idea of Imbued trying to use their abilities to confront mundane criminals and other social problems in addition to the supernatural. (My personal take on that question stems from a Justice League miniseries John Ostrander wrote, in which the Martian Manhunter points out that it's a good thing superheroes don't try to change the world by force, because they would inevitably clash over which changes to make. In terms of Hunter: The Reckoning, it makes a perfect reason to try to have some of them do it, as it will lead to conflicts that make great plot hooks.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:27:36-08:00","id":1180020,"title":"","content":"You know, Punisher as a wayward definitely makes sense. Also, with Demon Superheroes, I am not too familiar with it but is it a stretch to assume that showing random street crooks your demonic form will drive them incurably insane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:56:58-08:00","id":1180030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1180020#post1180020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, Punisher as a wayward definitely makes sense. Also, with Demon Superheroes, I am not too familiar with it but is it a stretch to assume that showing random street crooks your demonic form will drive them incurably insane?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Demon Form has different powers based on a variety of factors(which system you are using, what house you are, what lores you have, merits, flaws.. etc) I THINK there's a version that basically causes Delerium but nothing like &quot;you're incurably insane&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:00:52-08:00","id":1180051,"title":"","content":"Oh, thanks for telling me that. I am guessing that Reconcilers would be the most likely to be superheroes. I wonder how Demons would fight crooks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 01-28-2018, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T21:16:29-08:00","id":1180059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1180051#post1180051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, thanks for telling me that. I am guessing that Reconcilers would be the most likely to be superheroes. I wonder how Demons would fight crooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say its rather as simple as wanting to protect your thralls. Deciding to be &quot;the Devil of Hell's Kitchen&quot; having people come to you for favours and protect them from outsiders.. wouldn't be particular faction limiting. Well Ravagers probably wouldn't be ok...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T06:33:47-08:00","id":1180150,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that makes sense. The Devil of Hell's Kitchen sounds like a name of a Urban Legend told amongst the scum of the neighbourhood. In fact, that Fallen coud use that legend and let his Demonic appearance scare the shit out of crooks. Because, what crook in his right mind would actually try attacking a demon? Unless, he works for an Eartbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:26:51-08:00","id":1180278,"title":"","content":"Here is what i think what a Judge Imbued might look like as a Superhero: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gAY0jV6nGxs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gAY0jV6nGxs</a><br /> I also wonder what a Redeemer Imbued and a Martyr Imbued would be like as Superheroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:10:05-08:00","id":1180970,"title":"","content":"Someone already brought up Etherites and Akastics as good mage superheroes. I wonder what the rest of the Traditions, excluding the CoE and Dreamspeakers, would be like as superheroes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T19:41:59-08:00","id":1180983,"title":"","content":"Order of Hermes would be the likes of Dr. Strange, Zatana, Doctor Fate or Constantine, just adjusted to a more &quot;street-level&quot; style, sort of like the Dresden Files.<br /> Verbena would be like Madam Xanadu, Witchfire, some interpretations of the Scarlet Witch, and the like.<br /> Celestial Chorus would be like the Shining Knight (either version), Gabriel the Devil-Hunter, Rambam, or any character that fits the &quot;paladin&quot; archetype (Captain America, the Lone Ranger, etc.)<br /> <br /> Added: Virtual Adepts would be Spider Jerusalem from Transmetropolitan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-31-2018, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T17:35:45-08:00","id":1181287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1180983#post1180983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Order of Hermes would be the likes of Dr. Strange, Zatana, Doctor Fate or Constantine, just adjusted to a more &quot;street-level&quot; style, sort of like the Dresden Files.<br /> Verbena would be like Madam Xanadu, Witchfire, some interpretations of the Scarlet Witch, and the like.<br /> Celestial Chorus would be like the Shining Knight (either version), Gabriel the Devil-Hunter, Rambam, or any character that fits the &quot;paladin&quot; archetype (Captain America, the Lone Ranger, etc.)<br /> <br /> Added: Virtual Adepts would be Spider Jerusalem from Transmetropolitan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reasons i cut out the Cult and the Dreamspeakers is that i don't exactly think they would be superhero material. Since the Dreamspeakers are mostly invested in spirits i don't think they would be interested in fighting crime. With the CoE, who would really get ecstasy from beating the shit out of criminal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T18:19:58-08:00","id":1181297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1181287#post1181287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reasons i cut out the Cult and the Dreamspeakers is that i don't exactly think they would be superhero material. Since the Dreamspeakers are mostly invested in spirits i don't think they would be interested in fighting crime. With the CoE, who would really get ecstasy from beating the shit out of criminal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dreamspeakers are intermediaries between the material and the spiritual. The material effects the spiritual and vice versa. Wanting a place that is nicer by making it nicer is a pretty simple setup.. plus they have all sorts of mask themes.. I mean the weird symbolism of superheroes and villains probably makes more sense with a spiritual make up(&quot;I need to leave riddles because of my totem..&quot;)(&quot;I dress up like a bat because I have a pact with bat..&quot;)<br /> <br /> And you are profoundly misunderstanding the COX. Simply put they are about achieving an altered state of consciousness via extremity. This can be drugs, but it can easily be athletics or even deprivation. Fight Club would be an appropriate setup for COX members. Someone who finds meaning in the pain of his punches, the lack of sleep the actions drive him too all are part of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T19:07:02-08:00","id":1181308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1181297#post1181297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers are intermediaries between the material and the spiritual. The material effects the spiritual and vice versa. Wanting a place that is nicer by making it nicer is a pretty simple setup.. plus they have all sorts of mask themes.. I mean the weird symbolism of superheroes and villains probably makes more sense with a spiritual make up(&quot;I need to leave riddles because of my totem..&quot;)(&quot;I dress up like a bat because I have a pact with bat..&quot;)<br /> <br /> And you are profoundly misunderstanding the COX. Simply put they are about achieving an altered state of consciousness via extremity. This can be drugs, but it can easily be athletics or even deprivation. Fight Club would be an appropriate setup for COX members. Someone who finds meaning in the pain of his punches, the lack of sleep the actions drive him too all are part of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point on the CoX. Also, with the Dreamspeakers and the Totems i am already picturing a conversation with a Dreamspeaker hero and a normal human one. Here's how it goes.<br /> Hero: So, what exactly is your gimmick?<br /> Dreamspeaker: I have no gimmick, Hellcat. I am simply a Shaman working to improve the spirit world around this area.<br /> Hellcat: Sure you are. While your at it, why don't you do a dance right here. right now and bring in rain to wash away the blood these unconcious dimwits are leaking, (Notions to a group of KO'ed crooks.)<br /> DS: It dosen't work like that. By the way, have I told you that you're being followed ?<br /> HC: What are you talking about?<br /> DS: It seems like your actions has brought the attention of the great spirit, Coyote and it has sent one of it's avatars to observe you.<br /> Hc: Uhh, what's it doing now?<br /> DS: Laughing at your ridiculous costume.<br /> HC: Now i now your bullshitting!<br /> <br /> Also, with the VAs, i kinda pictured the main character from Watch Dog 1 or Neo from the Matrix. But, Spider works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T22:20:39-08:00","id":1181336,"title":"","content":"I've always thought the weird thematic gangs in Gotham and say the movie the Warriors make a certain amount of sense in an animistic cosmos, the chimage to totem on some level they make a certain amount of sense, it may even be something like &quot;I feel lucky like this&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T19:31:41-08:00","id":1181551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1181336#post1181336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought the weird thematic gangs in Gotham and say the movie the Warriors make a certain amount of sense in an animistic cosmos, the chimage to totem on some level they make a certain amount of sense, it may even be something like &amp;quot;I feel lucky like this&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea of Totems &quot;adopting&quot; some of these heroes. Besides Coyote, i wonder what totem would take interest in these heroes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T21:14:46-08:00","id":1181565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1181551#post1181551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do like the idea of Totems &quot;adopting&quot; some of these heroes. Besides Coyote, i wonder what totem would take interest in these heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spirits that are not Griffin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:36:28-08:00","id":1181727,"title":"","content":"Dreamspeakers: Besides the likes of Red Wolf, Black Crow, Brother Voodoo, Manitou Raven, Shaman, Talisman (both the original Aborigine one from Contest of Champions and the second First Nations one from Alpha Flight), Voodoo, T. Hawk (from Streetfighter) and the like, there's also Black Panther (if you strip away all the technology, he's still the spiritually empowered head priest of the Panther God as part of his role as tribal chief) and Jack Hawksmoor of the Authority (the so-called &quot;God of Cities&quot;, he effectively communes with the soul of urban areas, what in World of Darkness cosmology are called City Father/Mother/Other Incarnae). Also, Mike Grell's very short lived series Shaman's Tears from the very very early days of Image. I'm currently blanking on who was writing Spider-Man when they were pushing this &quot;avatar of the Spider-Totem&quot; thing, but that's also a possibility. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:49:40-08:00","id":1181739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1181551#post1181551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do like the idea of Totems &quot;adopting&quot; some of these heroes. Besides Coyote, i wonder what totem would take interest in these heroes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cockroach and Rat, maybe? Unicorn would be interesting. So would Pegasus (the character of Winged Victory from Astro City pretty much is this, in a sense, as that she's the chosen champion of a secret society of women who is empowered by the female half of the human race). <br /> <br /> Back when the Spider-Man books were doing the &quot;Spider-Totem&quot; thing, part of it was the implication that the bulk of his villains were also influenced by animal totems (vulture, rhino, chameleon, scorpion, octopus, lizard, kangaroo, gibbon, jackal, tarantula, grizzly, fly, cat, rabbit, rat, puma, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:58:10-08:00","id":1181786,"title":"","content":"Rat, Unicorn, Cockroah and Pegasus would be interesting totems. I wonder how these totems could contact their chosen heroes to make the &quot;adoption&quot; offer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 02-02-2018, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:54:37-08:00","id":1181832,"title":"","content":"I suppose crashing through a window while the hero is sitting there brooding wouldn't work. (&quot;The Joker is on the rampage. Someone go light the Roach-Signal!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Dream visitation maybe, or during a near death experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T18:22:09-08:00","id":1181878,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bI think dream visitation would be very interesting. I am now picturing a meeting between Unicorn and one of her new &quot;adopted&quot; children. Here's how that conversation will go.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bUnicorn: Hello, my child.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bHero: (Looks around his dream, eventually staring at Unicorn with wide eyes) What the hell!</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bUni: Calm down, I am not here to hurt you. I wish to give you an offer Malcom Crundel, or should I say, Highway Man.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b(At this moment, Malcom's clothing turns from a tank top and boxers to clothing that looks like it's straight from the 18th century, complete with a mask.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bHM: Alright, what is your offer.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bUni: I have seen you defend your community from drug dealers, mobsters and other vile aspects of society. Yet, your most recent action is what made me come to you. I saw you defend a child against his abusive father. That is what made me come to you. My offer is simple, I wish to sponsor you as your &quot;spirit guide&quot;.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hm: What will that mean?</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bUni: That would mean I will give you my blessings which will make your job as a defender easier. I will also be your guide and will give you advice when you need it. In exchange, you will have to defend the weak and helpless from those who will bring them harm.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bHm: (Thinks it over for a bit and turns to Unicorn with a smile) I accept your offer Unicorn.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bUni: Thank you. I will talk to you soon my child.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bNow I am wondering how the Changeing Breeds are going to react once Totems begin to adopt these humans?</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T17:54:54-08:00","id":1182132,"title":"","content":"I wonder if heroes &quot;adopted&quot; by totems will still be able to get gifts from them? Considering that they are most likely human. Also, I am wondering if groups like the Society of Leopold, Project Twilight and the Arcanum would have interest in these &quot;heroes&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T20:32:38-08:00","id":1182162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1182132#post1182132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if heroes &quot;adopted&quot; by totems will still be able to get gifts from them? Considering that they are most likely human. Also, I am wondering if groups like the Society of Leopold, Project Twilight and the Arcanum would have interest in these &quot;heroes&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not unless they made their superheroes kami.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T20:45:26-08:00","id":1182170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1182132#post1182132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if heroes &quot;adopted&quot; by totems will still be able to get gifts from them? Considering that they are most likely human. Also, I am wondering if groups like the Society of Leopold, Project Twilight and the Arcanum would have interest in these &quot;heroes&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory anyone can take the Totem background. Just anything that grants Gifts that run on Gnosis is basically useless, but any power that's innate or bonuses to skills.. It would actually be pretty subtle and even they may not know they are in a totem relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T21:10:20-08:00","id":1182174,"title":"","content":"Good point on the Gnosis issue. I guess that is why the totems could call themselves &quot;Spirit Guides&quot; for their &quot;adopted children. Also, i realized that those demon hunters, whose names ellude me right now, from KotE, could make awsome heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T19:53:20-08:00","id":1182477,"title":"","content":"I just found out that they are called Shih. Sorry for forgetting their names earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T22:27:03-08:00","id":1182502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1182477#post1182477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just found out that they are called Shih. Sorry for forgetting their names earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shih generally have one of two origins. Either they are orphaned by a monster and their master comes in to teach them. Or they are part of a lineage or secret village of Demon Hunters. Either way its pretty damned obvious how they'd work in a superhero setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T13:16:13-08:00","id":1182690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1182502#post1182502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Shih generally have one of two origins. Either they are orphaned by a monster and their master comes in to teach them. Or they are part of a lineage or secret village of Demon Hunters. Either way its pretty damned obvious how they'd work in a superhero setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, DHX said that there aren't any examples of the latter, but that individual games could assume that they exist. It only assumes that the former situation is how you become Shih - something bad happens to your family and/or other loved ones, you hold a grudge, and a scarred wanderer asks if you have the resolve to do something about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T20:34:07-08:00","id":1182789,"title":"","content":"I wonder what can convince a Shih to beat the shit out of thugs alongside slaying demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T00:33:27-08:00","id":1182829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1182789#post1182789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what can convince a Shih to beat the shit out of thugs alongside slaying demons?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a whole side bar on it but to summarize: Shih hunt Monsters. Being human doesn't stop you from being a monster. While Shen have better opportunities there's plenty of mortal wickedness.. and to be perfectly blunt Monster hunting doesn't pay the bills but large scale organized criminal syndicates well they tend to have alot of easily usable money on hand.. and well when you have a hammer...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T17:43:10-08:00","id":1183106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1182829#post1182829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's a whole side bar on it but to summarize: Shih hunt Monsters. Being human doesn't stop you from being a monster. While Shen have better opportunities there's plenty of mortal wickedness.. and to be perfectly blunt Monster hunting doesn't pay the bills but large scale organized criminal syndicates well they tend to have alot of easily usable money on hand.. and well when you have a hammer...</div> </div> </div> </div>I am picturing a moment where a Shih, who just arrived in America realizes that he needs money and beats up a bunch of gangbangers and steals all the cash from their wallets.<br /> <br /> Also, another idea i have for these heroes is for them to have petty rivalries amongst themselves, especially amongst the factions. This, of course leds to the type of violance they are trying to prevent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T20:23:20-08:00","id":1183141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1183106#post1183106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am picturing a moment where a Shih, who just arrived in America realizes that he needs money and beats up a bunch of gangbangers and steals all the cash from their wallets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd imagine it would be more they see them harassing a storeowner or something beat the hell out of them then just loot them..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, another idea i have for these heroes is for them to have petty rivalries amongst themselves, especially amongst the factions. This, of course leds to the type of violance they are trying to prevent. </div> </div> </div>They could divide up territory by their various groups, perhaps even &quot;request&quot; some form of financial support from the local businesses....<br /> <br /> <br /> That is to say there is a cycle of this &quot;vigilantes&quot; rise up in a local group to protect against the powerful and then become corrupted and become the criminal underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T18:44:51-08:00","id":1183457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1183141#post1183141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd imagine it would be more they see them harassing a storeowner or something beat the hell out of them then just loot them..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They could divide up territory by their various groups, perhaps even &quot;request&quot; some form of financial support from the local businesses....<br /> <br /> <br /> That is to say there is a cycle of this &quot;vigilantes&quot; rise up in a local group to protect against the powerful and then become corrupted and become the criminal underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of some of these groups becoming crooks themselves. Other reasons they fight each other could be different spirit &quot; guides&quot;, diffrences in crime fighting tactics all the the way to just disliking each other. Also, one think i didn't cover with Mage is the Disparates. I would think out of all the crafts in the Disparate Alliance the Templars and the Sisiter of Hippolyta would make the most sense as heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T19:15:03-08:00","id":1183459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1174885-help-developing-a-idea-superheroes?p=1183457#post1183457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of some of these groups becoming crooks themselves. Other reasons they fight each other could be different spirit &quot; guides&quot;, diffrences in crime fighting tactics all the the way to just disliking each other. Also, one think i didn't cover with Mage is the Disparates. I would think out of all the crafts in the Disparate Alliance the Templars and the Sisiter of Hippolyta would make the most sense as heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wu Lung pretty readily hit similar tropes as the Akashics and the Shih","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T01:33:55-08:00","id":1183509,"title":"","conten